{"schema":1,"language":"en","set":{"id":"swsh9tg","name":"Brilliant Stars Trainer Gallery","releaseDate":"2022-02-25","cardCount":{"official":30,"total":30}},"cards":[{"id":"swsh9tg-TG01","localId":"TG01","name":"Flareon","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"Once it has stored up enough heat, this Pokémon's body temperature can reach up to 1,700 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG02","localId":"TG02","name":"Vaporeon","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"When Vaporeon's fins begin to vibrate, it is a sign that rain will come within a few hours."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG03","localId":"TG03","name":"Octillery","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"It traps enemies with its suction-cupped tentacles, then smashes them with its rock-hard head."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG04","localId":"TG04","name":"Jolteon","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"If it is angered or startled, the fur all over its body bristles like sharp needles that pierce foes."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG05","localId":"TG05","name":"Zekrom","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"When the interior part of its tail spins like a motor, Zekrom can generate many bolts of lightning to blast its surroundings."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG06","localId":"TG06","name":"Dusknoir","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"At the bidding of transmissions from the spirit world, it steals people and Pokémon away. No one knows whether it has a will of its own."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG07","localId":"TG07","name":"Dedenne","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"Since Dedenne can't generate as much electricity on its own, it steals electricity from outlets or other electric Pokémon."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG08","localId":"TG08","name":"Alcremie","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"When Alcremie is content, the cream it secretes from its hands becomes sweeter and richer."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG09","localId":"TG09","name":"Ariados","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"It spews threads from its mouth to catch its prey. When night falls, it leaves its web to go hunt aggressively."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG10","localId":"TG10","name":"Houndoom","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"Identifiable by its eerie howls, people a long time ago thought it was the grim reaper and feared it."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG11","localId":"TG11","name":"Eevee","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"Thanks to its unstable genetic makeup, this special Pokémon conceals many different possible evolutions."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG12","localId":"TG12","name":"Oranguru","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"It knows the forest inside and out. If it comes across a wounded Pokémon, Oranguru will gather medicinal herbs to treat it."},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG13","localId":"TG13","name":"Boltund V","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false}},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG14","localId":"TG14","name":"Sylveon V","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false}},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG15","localId":"TG15","name":"Sylveon VMAX","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false}},{"id":"swsh9tg-TG16","localId":"TG16","name":"Mimikyu V","variants":{"normal":false,"holo"